WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.584
Your clients come in one by one with “New person”,

2
00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:09.679
from an Excel or CSV file with a duplicate check, as a contact list in “Prospecting”,

3
00:00:09.982 --> 00:00:12.999
or with the whole file of your previous CRM.

4
00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:18.870
In “Data & safety”, or in the setup wizard’s step, “Import clients”

5
00:00:18.871 --> 00:00:24.117
takes an .xlsx or .csv file, or rows you paste.

6
00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.670
You check which column is the name, phone or e-mail,

7
00:00:27.671 --> 00:00:30.921
and choose whether they come in as clients or prospects.

8
00:00:32.021 --> 00:00:35.108
Before anything is saved, each row shows as new,

9
00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:39.950
as someone already in AVRASTRO with the same phone, e-mail or name,

10
00:00:40.043 --> 00:00:45.371
even written in Greek or Latin letters, as repeated in the file, or with no name.

11
00:00:45.674 --> 00:00:47.705
Existing people are not changed,

12
00:00:47.891 --> 00:00:51.722
and the whole import can be undone with Ctrl+Z.

13
00:00:52.822 --> 00:00:55.619
In “Prospecting”, press “Import contacts”:

14
00:00:55.864 --> 00:00:59.671
choose a CSV or Excel file, or paste rows.

15
00:00:59.916 --> 00:01:00.624
Columns:

16
00:01:00.624 --> 00:01:05.836
name, phone, e-mail, occupation, company, area, source and notes;

17
00:01:06.023 --> 00:01:07.740
the header row is optional.

18
00:01:07.927 --> 00:01:10.108
From there, prospects become clients.

19
00:01:11.208 --> 00:01:15.178
If you used the earlier VÉRO CRM, go to “Data & safety”:

20
00:01:15.364 --> 00:01:18.092
“Choose backup file”, then “Analyze”.

21
00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:21.076
You see what is new, what changes and what

22
00:01:21.076 --> 00:01:23.641
stays the same, before anything is written.

23
00:01:23.944 --> 00:01:27.078
You choose merge, which is safe to re-import,

24
00:01:27.079 --> 00:01:30.445
or replace, and press “Import now”.

25
00:01:31.545 --> 00:01:34.389
Before the import a safety snapshot is taken,

26
00:01:34.482 --> 00:01:38.603
an integrity check runs, and at the end the import is verified.

27
00:01:38.848 --> 00:01:42.190
If verification fails, the changes are rolled back.

28
00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.566
For policies, “Policy from PDF”

29
00:01:45.566 --> 00:01:48.130
reads the insurer’s policy schedule on this device.

30
00:01:48.596 --> 00:01:51.892
Each value shows the line it came from, you check and correct it,

31
00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:55.468
and nothing is saved until you press “Save policy”.

32
00:01:56.568 --> 00:01:58.018
In the “Client list”

33
00:01:58.019 --> 00:02:00.898
you see every client, fill in what is missing,

34
00:02:01.084 --> 00:02:04.613
print it, or export it as CSV for Excel.
